Here's a little Perl script I hacked together that produces output like this:

> % nhk | head -10
> 1 812355 Medusa
> 1  75731 giant eel
> 7  41246 soldier ant
> 6  39322 mumak
> 6  29946 dwarf
> 2  25474 priest(ess)
> 2  22866 giant spider
> 5  20256 magic bolt
> 1  16757 poison spikes
> 1  15181 bugbear

The first number is the number of kills logged by a type of monster and the
second the combined score of all of its victims.  Command-line switches
let you sort by either number, and specify whether the logfile or the high
score list should be read.  In other words, it's a nethack high score list,
from the monsters' point of view.

Feedback would be appreciated.

John
